# The challenge's own SHA256SUMS is the byte-level authority, and every text
# artifact in the package is published with LF endings. A core.autocrlf=true
# checkout rewrites those files to CRLF on the way out, which breaks every
# published digest. Pinning eol=lf here stops the smudge at the source, so a
# fresh clone verifies clean.
#
# This file lives in the fork, not in the published package: it adds no bytes to
# any challenge artifact and changes no artifact blob.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary/large data: never convert, never diff as text.
*.bin -text
*.ct  -text
*.pkl -text

# The 44 published LPN samples are 720 MiB of hex rows that SHA256SUMS pins
# byte-for-byte. They are *data*, not prose: treating them as text costs a
# 720 MiB normalisation pass on every checkout, and a one-byte corruption then
# renders as "1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)" instead of a clear
# binary change. `-text` keeps the bytes verbatim; `-diff` keeps the diff honest.
lpn_samples/** -text -diff
